On Nov 19, 8:54 pm, Qwaszx86 <qwasz...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Through a series of mistakes, my pet became an invisible Quantum
> Mechanic, and I think he put on my dwarvish mythril armor. Is there
> anyway I can a) make him not invisible anymore or b) kill him without
> a penalty so I can get my armor back?

a) not that I've ever heard of, but you can gain the "see invisible"
intrinsic pretty readily.
b) there are lots of ways for a pet to die.  However, are you sure you
really need to get your armor back?  Can't you just find another set?
If you really want the armor though you could try wearing a ring of
conflict and herding your pet next to an aligned priest in a temple.
Alternatively, you could kill the pet yourself but recovering from the
penalty is potentially a longer road than just getting a new set of
armor.  If you do kill you pet be careful with prayer (i.e. make sure
you have positive luck/alignment before #praying) and be sure to not
have an uncursed or cursed luckstone as then bad luck won't timeout.
If you find an enemy with a breath weapon that also poses an
opportunity to kill your pet (reflection helps here).

My advice: don't worry about it; just move on and find yourself some
new armor.

